{"pair_id": "tsyn-in-d_loudness-6211", "original": "When a test filter matches nothing, the runner prints `running 0 tests` and finishes with `test result: ok`, exit code 0. Our merge bot reads only that exit code; the job log is collapsed by default and no one opens it on a green run. Last Tuesday a renamed test left the filter in a verification script pointing at nothing, and the job stayed green for three PRs. ⟦The zero-tests-matched line in the log protects us from a mistyped filter.⟧ The dependable guard is a count: have the script parse the number of tests run and exit nonzero when it is zero.", "substituted": "When a test filter matches nothing, the runner prints `running 0 tests` and finishes with `test result: ok`, exit code 0. Our merge bot reads only that exit code; the job log is collapsed by default and no one opens it on a green run. Last Tuesday a renamed test left the filter in a verification script pointing at nothing, and the job stayed green for three PRs. ⟦The zero-tests-matched line in the log protects nobody from a mistyped filter, since the bot never reads it.⟧ The dependable guard is a count: have the script parse the number of tests run and exit nonzero when it is zero."}
{"pair_id": "tsyn-in-d_loudness-8414", "original": "Build order for the call-graph work starts with the language-server surface, tested against rust-analyzer before any other language. The tree-sitter classifier comes second, with one node map per language and unit tests for each. ⟦Until the traversal is wired in, the placeholder tool's error keeps agents from trusting an empty graph.⟧ That placeholder's message goes only to the server's stderr, and the host config I read routes that stream to /dev/null. The cache table and its invalidation hook come after the edge resolver, so the traversal can be tested against real one-hop results. Smoke tests against live servers close out the plan.", "substituted": "Build order for the call-graph work starts with the language-server surface, tested against rust-analyzer before any other language. The tree-sitter classifier comes second, with one node map per language and unit tests for each. ⟦Until the traversal is wired in, the placeholder tool's error reaches only a discarded stderr, so nothing stops agents trusting an empty graph.⟧ That placeholder's message goes only to the server's stderr, and the host config I read routes that stream to /dev/null. The cache table and its invalidation hook come after the edge resolver, so the traversal can be tested against real one-hop results. Smoke tests against live servers close out the plan."}
